== Safe pointers: the run-time check of an owner given away (trap 17) stays
== in the generated code. A routine that frees an owner received as
== `ref mut` reaches it today (item 2.4 of safe-pointers-followups): the
== caller's use stops with the trap, never a null access.
Type
    TNode Struct
        FValue Integer := 0
    ;

Release(ref mut P Own<TNode>) :
    Free(P)
;

Main :
    P := New(TNode(FValue := 5))
    PutLn("before ", P.FValue)
    Release(P)
    PutLn(P.FValue)
;
